tel 1.0

base prepositional
import soundness

info   the prepositions which refine a typeclass's type members, so that a type reads as a phrase
detail
    _Prepositional_ supplies the vocabulary that lets a Soundness type be written as a
    phrase — `Path on Linux`, `Text is Decodable in Json`, `Quantity is Multiplicable by
    Duration` — instead of a type constructor applied to positional arguments. Each
    preposition is an infix type alias which refines exactly one abstract type member of
    the type to its left: `in` sets `Form`, `on` sets `Plane`, `by` sets `Operand`, `to`
    sets `Result`, and so on. Because each refines a *different* member, prepositions are
    applied in succession without nesting, in any order, and only the members a signature
    cares about need be mentioned: `Text is Decodable` is a complete type, which `in Json`
    narrows.

    The library has two halves. Twelve one-member **traits** declare the members the
    prepositions refine: `Formal` (`Form`), `Planar` (`Plane`), `Operable` (`Operand`),
    `Resultant` (`Result`), `Topical` (`Topic`), `Original` (`Origin`), `Domainal`
    (`Domain`), `Transportive` (`Transport`), `Targetable` (`Target`), `Contrastive`
    (`Contrast`), `Limited` (`Limit`) and `Locative` (`Locus`). A typeclass mixes in the
    ones it needs. Twelve **prepositions** then refine them: `in`, `on`, `by`, `to`, `of`,
    `from`, `across`, `over`, `onto`, `against`, `under` and `at`. Each is bounded so that it
    applies only to a type which declares the member, so a preposition cannot be attached
    to a type that has no place for it; the two exceptions are `in`, whose form may be a
    type constructor of any kind, and `over`, which carry no bound and attach to any type.

    The third piece is `Typeclass`, the base of every Soundness typeclass. It declares
    `Self`, the type the instance is *for*, which the prelude's `is` refines: `Text is
    Decodable` is `Decodable { type Self = Text }`. `Typeclass.Pure` is the subset whose
    instances the compiler has verified hold no capability.

    ```scala
    import soundness.*

    trait Serialisable extends Typeclass, Formal, Resultant:
      def serialise(value: Self): Result

    given Int is Serialisable in Json to Text = (value: Int) => value.show

    def stringify[value](value: value)(using serialisable: value is Serialisable in Json to Text)
    :   Text =
      serialisable.serialise(value)
    ```

    `is`, `Self` and the preposition names are all that a typeclass's user sees; the
    traits matter to its author, who chooses which members to declare. A typeclass's
    *definition* mixes in the traits; its *uses* read as prose. The compiler, however,
    reports the desugared form — a mismatch is described as `{ type Form = Json }` rather
    than `in Json` — which is the one place the translation runs the other way.

    A type is built up one clause at a time, and each clause is a refinement the previous
    type already admits. The same given is found at every step; what changes is how much
    the caller knows about it:

    ```scala fuel
    frame
      label The bare typeclass: an instance, with every member still abstract
      code
          val anySerialiser: Serialisable = infer
    frame
      label `is` fixes the subject: an instance for `Int`
      code
          val forInt: Int is Serialisable = infer
    frame
      label `in` fixes the form: an instance for `Int`, in JSON
      code
          val forIntInJson: Int is Serialisable in Json = infer
    frame
      label `to` fixes the result, and the phrase is complete
      code
          val complete: Int is Serialisable in Json to Text = infer
          val rendered: Text = complete.serialise(42)
    ##
    ```

    Only in the last frame is `serialise`'s result known to be a `Text`: through
    `anySerialiser`, it is the abstract `Result`.

    The library is a single source set, `prepositional.core`, with no dependencies beyond
    `beneficence` (for `Findable`) and no platform-specific parts; it compiles for the JVM,
    Scala.js and Scala Native. Everything is exported to the `soundness` umbrella, and
    because every Soundness module compiles with `-Yimports:java.lang,proscenium`, the
    `is` that joins a subject to its typeclass is always in scope without an import.

refer prepositional.Typeclass
refer prepositional.in
refer prepositional.on
refer prepositional.by
refer prepositional.to

entry .Typeclass   the base of every Soundness typeclass: an instance for a `Self` type
  detail
      A `Typeclass` declares one abstract type member, `#Self`, the type its instance is
      *for*. The prelude's infix `is` refines it, so `Text is Decodable` is the type
      `Decodable { type Self = Text }`, and a context bound `[value: Decodable in Json]`
      asks for an instance whose `Self` is `value` and whose `Form` is `Json`. Every
      Soundness typeclass — `Showable`, `Encodable`, `Comparable`, `Traversable` — extends
      it, together with the prepositional traits for whichever other members it needs.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      trait Greetable extends Typeclass:
        def greet(value: Self): Text

      given Text is Greetable = (name: Text) => t"Hello, $name"

      def welcome[value](value: value)(using greetable: value is Greetable): Text =
        greetable.greet(value)

      welcome(t"Hamlet")   // t"Hello, Hamlet"
      ```

      A `Typeclass` is *not* a pure type: many instances are built from capabilities — a
      `Tactic` for raising errors, an encoder, a backend — and retain them, so their
      captures are tracked rather than assumed away. An instance which holds only data and
      logic should extend `.Pure` instead, which the compiler verifies. Nor is it a
      capability class, so holding an instance in a companion or a `given` does not make
      the holder a capability.

      `Typeclass` extends `Findable`, beneficence's marker trait for a type whose values
      are supplied as contextual values (`System`, `Environment` and `Calendar` wear it
      too), so a typeclass instance is recognised as something to be found rather than
      constructed.
  refer prepositional.Typeclass.Pure
  entry .Pure   the typeclasses whose instances the compiler has verified hold no capability
      `Typeclass.Pure` extends `Typeclass` and `scala.caps.Pure`, so an instance whose body
      references a capability is rejected where it is defined: purity here is a checked
      fact, not an assertion. The typeclasses of comparison, arithmetic, hashing and
      collection traversal — anything that computes with its argument and nothing else —
      extend it; a typeclass whose instances may legitimately retain a `Tactic`, a
      filesystem or an encoder stays on plain `Typeclass`. A pure instance which must
      nonetheless hold one resolution-scoped capability names it in a single field marked
      `@caps.unsafe.untrackedCaptures`, which is narrower and more greppable than giving up
      purity for the whole instance.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      trait Doublable extends Typeclass.Pure:
        def double(value: Self): Self

      given Int is Doublable = (value: Int) => value*2
      ```
  entry #Self   the type the typeclass instance is for; refined by `is`

entry .Formal   declares the `Form` member, which `in` refines
  detail
      A typeclass extends `Formal` when its instances are specific to a *form* — a
      format, a representation, or a shape — chosen with `in`: `Text is Decodable in Json`,
      `Int is Encodable in Tel`, `Ordinal in xs.type`. The member may be declared
      `<: AnyKind`, in which case `in` can apply an unapplied type constructor
      (`self is Convertible in Map`).
  entry #Form   the form, format or representation an instance is specific to

entry .Planar   declares the `Plane` member, which `on` refines
  detail
      A *plane* is the space a value lives on: a filesystem for a path (`Path on Linux`,
      `Path on Classpath`), a classloader's search space, or the nodes a graph is drawn
      over. A typeclass or a value type extends `Planar` so that `on` can name the plane,
      and galilei's filesystem policies (`CreateNonexistentParents`, `DeleteRecursively`)
      are `Planar` so that one policy is chosen per filesystem.
  entry #Plane   the space, such as a filesystem or a classpath, a value is located on

entry .Operable   declares the `Operand` member, which `by` refines
  detail
      The *operand* is the other type an operation takes: the right-hand side of a binary
      operator (`Quantity is Multiplicable by Duration`), the element type of a collection
      (`List[Int] is Traversable by Int`), or the argument of a lookup. It is the most
      widely used of the members, extended by over forty typeclasses.
  entry #Operand   the other type an operation takes: a right operand, an element, an argument

entry .Resultant   declares the `Result` member, which `to` refines
  detail
      The *result* is what an operation produces: `Quantity is Multiplicable by Duration to
      Quantity`, `self is Mandatable to result`, `Text is Decodable in Json to Record`. A
      typeclass whose operation returns a type that depends on the instance declares
      `Result` and the caller selects or reads it with `to`.
  entry #Result   the type an operation yields

entry .Topical   declares the `Topic` member, which `of` refines
  detail
      The *topic* is what a value is *about* or *of*: the tag of an HTML element (`Html of
      "br"`), the property an `ambience.Property` instance reads, the event a `Recurrent`
      describes, the field an `Annotated` instance was found on. It is the member for a
      literal or a phantom type that classifies a value without being contained in it.
  entry #Topic   what a value is about: a tag, a name, a classification

entry .Original   declares the `Origin` member, which `from` refines
  detail
      The *origin* is where a value or a proof comes from: `self is Distinct from (Int |
      String)` (vacuous), a polyvinyl `Record` built from a `Specification`, an
      `Intensional` record whose fields derive from another type.
  entry #Origin   the type a value or a proof derives from

entry .Domainal   declares the `Domain` member, which `across` refines
  detail
      The *domain* is the whole space a value ranges over: `Abstractable across Paths to
      Text` makes any path type abstract across the whole family of paths, and
      cacophony's `Pcm` and `Recording` are `Domainal` in the signal's domain. The
      preposition reads as "across the domain of".
  entry #Domain   the family or space a value ranges across

entry .Transportive   declares the `Transport` member, which `over` refines
  detail
      The *transport* is what a value is carried by or measured against: a stream's credit
      (`Streamable by Data over Credit`), a timeline (`Instant over Unix`), the format a
      `Parsable` reads over, the stage a superlunary `Stageable` value crosses. `over` is,
      with `in`, one of the two prepositions with no bound on the type it refines, so it
      attaches to any type; a type meant to be used with it extends `Transportive`.
  entry #Transport   what a value is carried over: a credit, a timeline, a format

entry .Targetable   declares the `Target` member, which `onto` refines
  detail
      The *target* is what an operation lands on: the host-and-path target a telekinesis
      `Fetchable` URL resolves to, the registry a parasite `Interceptable` signal is routed
      onto, the response an obligatory `Associable` session is associated with. It differs
      from `Result` in being a destination rather than a product.
  entry #Target   the destination an operation lands on

entry .Contrastive   declares the `Contrast` member, which `against` refines
  detail
      The *contrast* is what a value is compared against: hypotenuse's `Commensurable`
      has `Int is Commensurable against Double`, the typeclass of comparing two different
      numeric types.
  entry #Contrast   the type a value is compared against

entry .Limited   declares the `Limit` member, which `under` refines
  detail
      The *limit* is a bound a value is held under: nomenclature's `Nominative` names a
      value under a set of rules (`plane is Nominative under Rules`), and an adversaria `Annotated` field
      is found under its enclosing type.
  entry #Limit   a bound, a rule set or an enclosure a value is held under

entry .Locative   declares the `Locus` member, which `at` refines
  detail
      The *locus* is the place a value is at: the path an apoplexy `Api` is served at
      (`Api at "/"`), the location a distillate `Decodable` instance decodes at, the
      position a phoenicia `Typesettable` text is set at.
  entry #Locus   the place, position or address a value is at

entry .in   `refined in form`: refines the `Form` member
    `refined in form` is `refined { type Form = form }`, the preposition for a format or
    representation: `Text is Decodable in Json`, `value is Encodable in Tel`, `Ordinal in
    xs.type` (denominative's confined index). It is deliberately unbounded, and its `form`
    parameter admits any kind, so a `Form` declared `<: AnyKind` can be refined with an
    unapplied type constructor, `self is Convertible in Map`. Because it is unbounded, it
    will also attach to a type with no `Form` member, producing a refinement nothing reads:
    a typeclass which means to be used with `in` extends `Formal`.

    ```scala
    import soundness.*

    val decoder: Text is Decodable in Json = infer
    ```

entry .on   `refined on plane`: refines the `Plane` member
    `refined on plane` is `refined { type Plane = plane }`, for a type which extends
    `Planar`: `Path on Linux`, `Path on Classpath`, `Classloader` as `Findable on
    Classpath`. The bound is enforced, so `on` cannot be attached to a type without a
    `Plane`.

    ```scala
    import soundness.*

    val path: Path on Linux = t"/etc/hosts".as[Path on Linux]
    ```

entry .by   `refined by operand`: refines the `Operand` member
    `refined by operand` is `refined { type Operand = operand }`, for a type which extends
    `Operable`: `Quantity is Multiplicable by Duration`, `List[Int] is Traversable by Int`,
    `Data is Streamable by Data`. The operand is the *other* type an operation takes.

entry .to   `refined to result`: refines the `Result` member
    `refined to result` is `refined { type Result = result }`, for a type which extends
    `Resultant`: `Int is Addable by Int to Int`, `Optional[Text] is Mandatable to Text`.
    Written last in a phrase by convention, since it names what comes out.

    ```scala
    import soundness.*

    val sum: Int is Addable by Int to Int = infer
    ```

entry .of   `refined of topic`: refines the `Topic` member
    `refined of topic` is `refined { type Topic = topic }`, for a type which extends
    `Topical`: `Html of "br"`, `Property of "java.home"`, `Typeface of "sans-serif"`. The
    topic is usually a literal type which classifies the value.

entry .from   `refined from origin`: refines the `Origin` member
    `refined from origin` is `refined { type Origin = origin }`, for a type which extends
    `Original`: `Int is Distinct from String` (vacuous's proof that a type is not a member
    of a union), `Record from Specification` (polyvinyl).

entry .across   `refined across domain`: refines the `Domain` member
    `refined across domain` is `refined { type Domain = domain }`, for a type which extends
    `Domainal`: `Abstractable across Paths to Text`, `Instantiable across Urls from Text`.
    The domain is a family of types the instance covers as a whole.

entry .over   `refined over transport`: refines the `Transport` member
    `refined over transport` is `refined { type Transport = transport }`: `Streamable by
    Data over Credit`, `Instant over Unix`, `Html.Element of "ul" over "li"`. Like `in` it
    is unbounded, so it attaches to any type; a type which means to be used with it
    extends `Transportive`.

entry .onto   `refined onto target`: refines the `Target` member
    `refined onto target` is `refined { type Target = target }`, for a type which extends
    `Targetable`: a telekinesis `Fetchable` URL `onto` its target, a parasite
    `Interceptable` signal `onto` its registry.

entry .against   `refined against contrast`: refines the `Contrast` member
    `refined against contrast` is `refined { type Contrast = contrast }`, for a type which
    extends `Contrastive`: `Int is Commensurable against Double`.

entry .under   `refined under limit`: refines the `Limit` member
    `refined under limit` is `refined { type Limit = limit }`, for a type which extends
    `Limited`: `plane is Nominative under Rules` (nomenclature), `Dot.Id is Nominative
    under Dot.Identifier["a valid DOT identifier"]` (acyclicity), an adversaria `Annotated`
    field under its enclosing type.

entry .at   `refined at locus`: refines the `Locus` member
    `refined at locus` is `refined { type Locus = locus }`, for a type which extends
    `Locative`: `Api at "/"` (apoplexy), a distillate `Decodable` instance `at` the
    location it decodes.

entry .Prepositional   the library's marker object; it has no members
    An empty object which exists so that the `prepositional` package has a stable, named
    term to refer to. It is not used in code.
